  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical and financial assistance for the reconstruction of Muzibu-Az</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tombs of Buganda Kings at Kasubi World Heritage property was added to the List of World Heritage in Danger in 2010 following a devastating fire at the Muzibu-Azaala-Mpanga, which housed the four tombs of the Buganda Kings and is considered an architectural masterpiece. 
This Japanese Funds-in-Trust project is offering Emergency Assistance to the State Party of Uganda and accompany them in rehabilitating the property in view of its removal from the List of World Heritage in Danger.</narrative>
  </description>
